t card arrives whole (sentences 38 px) with a picture from its first frame. The picture is answer-free: nothing on it can be counted, measured or read off to get the answer. Method aids (ledgers, formula strips, memory cards) are hidden while a countdown runs; every supplied value and condition stays on the card. Each feedback scene keeps a navy givens strip from its first frame.\n- **Notes scene.** Five one-line bullets (95 characters or fewer, 34 px, role colours), the framed memory card beside them, and a notes scene of 45 s in all.\n- **Slip arrows keep their red.** The red dashed slip arrows show which way the car would slide; that is a subject meaning in this design's colour key, not a mistake mark. Mistakes still take the slate scribble (R1).\n\n## Script and shots\n\nCue words in **bold** trigger the visual change. Exact frames are set from the recording's word timings. Screen symbols in italic: *N*, *m*, *g*, *θ*, *f*, *v*, *r*, *v_design*. Paper background and handwritten headline face as the explainer house style.\n\n",
